       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and the FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose or formulation**, such as extended-release, which is usually capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you want, please confirm that it is intentional. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first. I can add that confirmation to the order note."
      }
